From: idiazraz <100824525+idiazraz@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: tag PPE flows to the GPON port on AN7581 too

The CPU path tags every frame for a GPON port with its GEM port ID,
T-CONT channel and queue on each SoC with gpon_metadata (EN7523 and
AN7581). The PPE only filled those fields on EN7523, so on AN7581 a
bound upstream flow left through GDM2 with no GEM tag and channel 2.
The OLT never saw those frames: once TCP's upstream ACKs bound, the
download stalled at a few KB/s.

Gate the GPON metadata on gpon_metadata, the same test the CPU path
uses. The FOE fields match the vendor SDK for AN7581: EtherType
carries the GEM ID, channel and NBQ the T-CONT.
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
@@ -660,7 +660,11 @@
 				return -EINVAL;
 			}
 
-			if (airoha_is(eth, airoha_en7523) &&
+			/* Every SoC whose CPU path tags GPON frames (EN7523,
+			 * AN7581) needs the same GEM/T-CONT tags in the FOE,
+			 * or bound upstream frames leave untagged and are lost.
+			 */
+			if (eth->soc->gpon_metadata &&
 			    (dev->flags & AIROHA_PRIV_F_XPON_MANAGED) &&
 			    dev->xpon_mode == AIROHA_XPON_MODE_GPON) {
 				int ret;
@@ -784,7 +788,7 @@
 		l2->etype = BIT(dsa_port);
 		l2->etype |= !data->vlan.num ? BIT(15) : 0;
 	} else if (xpon_flow) {
-		/* EN7523 reuses the FOE EtherType field as the GPON GEM tag. */
+		/* The FOE EtherType field carries the GPON GEM tag. */
 		l2->etype = xpon.gem_port_id;
 	} else if (data->pppoe.num) {
 		l2->etype = ETH_P_PPP_SES;
